course: dictionary
lesson: 13480
title: Short forms: ICU
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are shortened to a few capital letters. These are called abbreviations. ICU is one of them, and it is used a lot in hospital stories and on the news. «The nurses in the ICU check the patient every hour.» The letters stand for words, and the context tells you what they mean here: a place where nurses look after very ill people.
explain: Read the words around the abbreviation to work out its meaning. «Mum's friend has been in ICU since the accident.» The word «accident» and the idea of a patient being cared for tell you this is serious. An ICU is the part of a hospital where very ill or badly hurt patients get constant care and special machines to help them breathe and keep their heart working.
explain: Some letters also appear in other short forms. «The baby was taken to the NICU because she was born very early.» Here the N means neonatal, which means for new babies. «The PICU has beds for children» uses P for paediatric, which means for children. Once you know the pattern, you can read new short forms more easily.
explain: The same letters can mean something different in a text message. «Sam texted: "icu"» does not mean a hospital here. It is informal texting slang for «I see you». Always check the context before you decide what a short form means. Ask yourself: is this a hospital story, or a message between friends?
fact: ICU stands for «intensive care unit».
fact: ICU is usually written in capital letters.
fact: In the UK, an ICU is also called «intensive care» or «ITU».
fact: PICU means paediatric ICU, for children; NICU means neonatal ICU, for new babies.
fact: In texting, informal «icu» can mean «I see you».
exercise: «The nurses in the ICU check the patient every hour.» What does ICU stand for? | ice cream unit | *intensive care unit | international cookery university | interesting cat umbrella
exercise: «The baby went to the NICU because she was born early.» What does NICU mean? | *neonatal intensive care unit, for new babies | new kitchen, for cooking | nurses in cold uniforms | a noisy internet club
exercise: Maya gets a text that just says «icu». What does her friend most likely mean? | Intensive care unit | *I see you | Are you hungry? | I am very ill
test: «The PICU has beds for children who are very ill.» What does PICU stand for? | public information care unit | play and ice cream unit | pretty interesting cat unit | *paediatric intensive care unit
test: Dad says, «Grandma is in ITU now.» What does ITU mean in the UK? | Internet time unit | Interesting train universe | *Intensive care unit | Ice tea unit
exam: What does the short form PICU mean in a hospital story? | Play and ice cream unit | Pretty interesting cat unit | Public information care unit | *Paediatric intensive care unit, for children
